 | Chairman & CEO | Age 57 | Compensation: $3.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 104 people. Revenue per employee of $4.5M ranks in the above the sector median among Real Estate peers. Each employee generates $787K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $114K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Urban Edge Properties is a mid-cap real estate business with a $2.9B market cap on $472M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 9% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $82M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 17 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.95\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 2.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 100% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $3.9M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-3921461.1},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 15% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 22% margin of safety against estimated fair value","11 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Real Estate peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Urban Edge Properties (UE) Could Be 11% Undervalued After Its Guidance Upgrade","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-ue/urban-edge-properties/news/urban-edge-properties-ue-could-be-11-undervalued-after-its-g","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794586542.249,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.718,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance","analyst_action"]},{"title":"Astronergy impulsa el mayor proyecto de energa renovable terrestre de la UE junto a Rezolv Energy en Rumania","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/astronergy