t 5.8% over 3 years, 7.4% over 5 years and 3.9% over 10 years, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 13%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded -0.6% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: FFO growth of 10.1% a year over five years.","Capex runs only 0.7x depreciation (21.4% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 22, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.1%), and institutions hold 100%.","It returns 3.3% a year to shareholders (4.0% in dividends).","The share count has grown 1.5% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It has paid a dividend for 11 consecutive years, raising it 29.1% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 104 employees, each generates about $4.5M of revenue, 2.0x the Real Estate median, and revenue has grown 3.9% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $787K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.2M (1x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $114K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":65,"head":"Watch: interest coverage only 2.3x.","pros":["Trades 22% below fair value of $26.76","FCF margin 17.3%","Revenue grew 7.4%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA -0.2x","Returns 3.3% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Interest coverage only 2.3x","P/FCF 35.1x vs sector 17.8x"],"flags":[],"need":["its composite (37) is below 39"],"buy_below":22.75,"vc":{"base":26.76,"base_src":"dcf","bear":19.96,"bull":36.44,"alt_median":8.41,"n_alt":3,"gap":2.1805,"dispersion":0.4349,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (43% dispersion)","DCF is 218% above the other models' median ($8.41)"]},"med":{"pe":23.8785,"ev_ebitda":16.1705,"pfcf":17.849,"pb":1.3551,"roic":0.0405,"gross_margin":